A good strategy is to drop unidentified stuff that might be junk or
might be useful (scrolls/potions/books/&c) in a protected/concealed
stash somewhere and come back to it when you have the means of
identifying a bunch of stuff.  A good place would be under a boulder
in the first sokoban level or in a box/chest/bag that's protected from
engulfing monsters.

> c - I'm not sure if I'm in the main cave or not. Is there any way of
> knowing? (is it enough to see if it's "cavelike" or "room+corridor").

The main branch is room+corridoer.  Early on, there are two side
branches (and you'll want to visit both).  One leads downward and is
cavelike in arrangement.  There is always a town with a temple in this
branch.  The other leads upwards and features boulders and pits
between you and the upstair.

